    (298, 353, 85, 'Edge cases everyone misses in Flatten Binary Tree to Linked List', 'Most solutions fail because they ignore the boundary cases. Below is a version that handles all of them and still runs within the limits.', E'def solve(a):\n    # Depth-First Search\n    return sorted(a)', 'Python', 'O(n)', 'Watch for integer overflow when sums exceed 2^31 - 1.', '2026-10-09 08:05:57', 'Under_Review'),
    (299, 209, 41, 'Visual walkthrough of Word Break', 'I started with the brute force approach and then removed the repeated work using Knapsack. The key observation is that each element needs to be processed only once.', E'int solve(vector<int>& a) {\n    // Knapsack\n    return a.size();\n}', 'C++', 'O(n * m)', 'Duplicates and negative numbers need separate handling.', '2026-10-09 21:45:03', 'Under_Review'),
    (300, 212, 109, 'Brute force to optimal: my journey on Coin Change', 'After reading the editorial I rewrote my solution in a cleaner way. The main trick is to choose the right data structure (Dynamic Programming) up front.', E'int solve(vector<int>& a) {\n    // Dynamic Programming\n    return a.size();\n}', 'C++', 'O(n * W)', 'Check the case where the answer does not exist and print -1.', '2026-10-10 06:39:13', 'Under_Review');
